_AP = {
 "Experimental Frame": "A sophisticated exo-suit that boosts your strength and shelters you. It counts as heavy armor you can don or doff as a bonus action, it grants the benefits of a life suit, you are proficient with it, and nobody else can wear it. While you wear it: your size is Medium if smaller, and your speed is 30 ft if lower. Your AC is 10 + Dexterity modifier + Intelligence modifier, and the armor cannot be enchanted or modified to improve AC. At the start of each turn you gain temporary hit points equal to your gadgeteer level, lasting until you remove the frame. You can integrate a simple or martial weapon into the frame, or two weapons (one per arm) if neither is Two-Handed. An integrated weapon snaps to your hand and you cannot be disarmed of it. You are proficient with integrated weapons while in the frame. When you attack with an integrated melee weapon, you can use Intelligence instead of Strength or Dexterity for attack and damage rolls. You can change integrated weapons after a Long Rest. From level 5, when you make a melee attack with an integrated weapon, you can make an extra melee attack with it as a bonus action.",
 "Mechanized Autonomous Construct": "A custom automaton piloted by your AI, a MAC. It takes its own turn right after yours. On your turn you can mentally command it within 500 ft with no action, choosing its action and movement, or giving a general command such as guarding a corridor. In combat its actions follow its Combat Protocols, which you can switch as a bonus action. If you are incapacitated or absent, your AI guides it to protect you and itself. At 0 hit points it is disabled. A Long Rest repairs it to full, and you always have enough materials. You can integrate one two-handed melee weapon, two one-handed melee weapons, or one one-handed melee weapon and a gadget. An integrated item snaps to its hand and it cannot be disarmed of it. It is proficient with integrated weapons and uses the Use an Object action to activate an integrated gadget. From level 5, it makes two attacks instead of one when you command the Attack action with integrated weapons.",
 "Utility Matrix": "A cube-shaped mechanism that rearranges into other devices. You can use these at will. Cloaking Device: as an action, warp the light around you and become Invisible until the start of your next turn, or until you attack, cast a spell or use a gadget. Not usable on the following round. Flashbang: as a bonus action, throw a concussive bomb at your feet. Each creature within 5 ft cannot take reactions until the start of its next turn. Not usable on the following round. Forcefield Projector: as a bonus action, until the start of your next turn your AC rises by your Intelligence modifier. Not usable on the following round. Grappling Hook: as a reaction when you fall, or as a bonus action, project a hook to a spot you see within your speed. If it can hold your weight, you are pulled there, spending movement normally, with no opportunity attacks. Not usable on the following round. Modular Gadget: from level 5, reconfigure the matrix into an un-upgraded gadget of your choice with no prerequisites. It does not count against gadgets known. Or reconfigure it into an upgrade for a gadget you have and qualify for. Long Rest before reconfiguring again."
}
